-its DRAM path. Slack orders admission but does not scale a request's
-footprint. Admitting whole footprints makes accounting and updates
-predictable under noisy estimates, at the cost of possible unused
-capacity or missed gains from partial protection. It is a policy choice,
-not an optimality claim or a serial recovery order.
+\begin{figure}[t]
+  \raggedright
+  \refstepcounter{designalgorithm}\label{alg:slack-estimation}
+  \noindent\textbf{Algorithm \thedesignalgorithm: GBDT--CPM slack estimation}
+  \par\smallskip
+  \noindent Input: $G_t$, visible features $x(t)$, GBDT $f_\theta$, live
+  requests $\mathcal R_t$, and segment map $a(r)$.
+  Output: request slack $\sigma$.
+  \par\smallskip
+  \begin{tabularx}{\columnwidth}{@{}r@{\quad}X@{}}
+    \toprule
+     1 & $\sigma_r\gets0$ for all $r\in\mathcal R_t$ \\
+     2 & \textbf{if} DAG structure incomplete: \textbf{return} $\sigma$ \\
+     3 & $z_a\gets f_\theta(x_a(t))$ for all $a\in V_t$ \\
+     4 & \textbf{if} any prediction unavailable or invalid: \textbf{return} $\sigma$ \\
+     5 & $\widehat d_a\gets\max(\varepsilon,z_a)\ \forall a$; $\pi\gets\mathrm{Topo}(G_t)$ \\
+     6 & \textbf{for} $a$ in $\pi$: \\
+     7 & \quad $\mathrm{EF}_a\gets\widehat d_a+\max_{b\in P(a)}\mathrm{EF}_b$ \\
+     8 & $T\gets\max(\{0\}\cup\{\mathrm{EF}_a:a\in V_t\})$ \\
+     9 & \textbf{for} $a$ in reverse $\pi$: \\
+    10 & \quad $\mathrm{LF}_a\gets\min_{b\in S(a)}(\mathrm{LF}_b-\widehat d_b)$ \\
+    11 & \textbf{for} $r\in\mathcal R_t$: \\
+    12 & \quad $\sigma_r\gets\max(0,\mathrm{LF}_{a(r)}-\mathrm{EF}_{a(r)})$ \\
+    13 & \textbf{return} $\sigma$ \\
+    \bottomrule
+  \end{tabularx}
+  \par\smallskip
+  \noindent $P(a)$/$S(a)$: predecessors/successors. Empty predecessor
+  max is $0$; empty successor min is $T$; $\varepsilon>0$ is a
+  minimum remaining-time floor.
+  \Description{GBDT predicts remaining agent-segment durations. Forward
+    CPM computes earliest finishes and the workflow horizon; backward
+    CPM computes latest finishes. Requests inherit their segment's slack.
+    Incomplete dependency structure or unavailable predictions return zero slack.}
+\end{figure}
+
+\paragraph{Propagate and refresh slack.}
+The forward pass computes earliest finishes relative to now; the
+backward pass computes latest finishes without extending horizon $T$.
+Their difference is the segment slack inherited by its live requests.
+This shared margin is not an independent allowance for every request.
+Request arrivals/completions, DAG updates, and placement windows trigger
+refreshes; CPM costs $O(|V_t|+|E_t|)$. Unknown dependency structure or missing
+predictions force zero slack for that workflow. These are planning
+estimates, not delay guarantees: Figure~\ref{fig:design-insights}(\subref{fig:insight-agent-time})
+audits episode prediction but does not validate the complete Tracker.
